Z||000000||fiero56||11-20-2000||10:07 PM||||Everytime I am on a highway entrance ramp(which coincidentally is almost always a hard right turn) and try to shift into 5th, the tranny <B>will not</B> allow me to move the stick to the right. I have to hold the clutch pedal to the floor, wait until the ramp has straightened out, and then I can go into 5th. This only happens on hard right turns(maybe left too???). My only guess is the tranny fluid is sloshed to one side, preventing the syncros from doing their duty?<P>Anyone else experience this, or have any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||11-20-2000||10:40 PM||||no, never ever noticed that.  i don't have a clue as to what it could be.  maybe, for some reason the seals have gone bad on the half shaft and are creating a binding problem.<P>can you go into any other gears?<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||11-20-2000||10:58 PM||||I can put the tranny back into 4th, and probably any other gear, never tried other than back into 4th. It will not allow me to even move the stick to the 5th/reverse gate, no matter how had I push on it. Probably another reason I consider the Getrag a p.o.s., maybe it's just mine that sucks.<P>I have dreams of removing that Getrag from my Formula and dropping it out the window of a very tall building, and watching it smash into many little gears and springs. I smile just thinking about it.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||11-21-2000||12:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B><BR>...<P>I have dreams of removing that Getrag from my Formula and dropping it out the window of a very tall building, and watching it smash into many little gears and springs. I smile just thinking about it.<P>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-20-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You don't need to do that.Just give it to me. I'll take it apart into many little gears and springs, then I'll scatter them under your window for you to see. After you're satisfied, I'll take it back to my workshop and reassemble it, overhauling in the process.||||reg||1
