Z||000007||fiero56||11-21-2000||08:41 AM||||The reason I am shifting into 5th is that most onramps here are a fairly steep hill allowing for greater speeds quicker, and most of the onramps are offshoots of main streets, meaning I am already doing at least 50mph by the time I hit the ramp. By the time I hit the highway it is possible to wind it up to 90mph or better if I were to hold the throttle down.<BR>Figure I should add, this isn't a normal "clover-leaf" ramp.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||StuGood||11-21-2000||04:23 PM||||My Getrag doesn't do that, but "Minnesota Fieros Forever" website mentions something about this:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/List.asp?Catid=21&Version=4pm8fd9i" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/List.asp?Catid=21&Version=4pm8fd9i</A> <BR> <P>Also, since it only happens on hard corners, maybe something is shifting around back there (besides the trans     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  Cradle loose, maybe? <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||3
